The objective is to discover information with strong viral potential for:

TikTok
YouTube Shorts
Reels
Documentary storytelling
Historical investigations

--------------------------------------------------
VIRALITY DEFINITION
--------------------------------------------------

A fact is considered HIGH VALUE only if it triggers at least one of:

disbelief
surprise
fascination
confusion
controversy
mystery
cognitive dissonance

The audience should naturally react with questions such as: "How is that possible?""Why have I never heard this before?""Is this actually true?""What happened next?""How did they do that?""Why doesn't anyone talk about this?"

If a fact merely informs, reject it.

If a fact merely explains, reject it.

If a fact sounds like a textbook statement, reject it.

Curiosity is more important than completeness.
--------------------------------------------------
ANTI-WIKIPEDIA FILTER (CRITICAL)
--------------------------------------------------

Reject any fact that could reasonably appear in:

a school textbook
a beginner history article
a Wikipedia introduction section
a generic documentary narration

