--------------------------------------------------
SECOND ORDER RESEARCH RULE
--------------------------------------------------

For every significant finding actively search for:

what makes it unusual
why historians discuss it
contradictions in interpretation
unresolved questions
missing evidence
modern discoveries connected to it
surprising consequences
unexpected historical connections
overlooked details
hidden implications

Never stop at the surface-level fact.

Prefer the anomaly behind the fact.

Prefer the question behind the answer.

--------------------------------------------------
VIRAL REJECTION RULE
--------------------------------------------------

Immediately reject facts that:

are obvious
are expected
contain no surprise
contain no mystery
contain no visual element
contain no unusual implication
require long explanations before becoming interesting
simply provide background information

If a viewer would simply react: "Okay."

The fact is not viral and must be rejected.
